  abstract = {Analysis of No Child Left Behind testing data found that accountability systems based on proficiency thresholds created perverse incentives to focus resources on students near the threshold ("bubble kids") while neglecting both high-performing and low-performing students. The paper estimates that 10-25\% of measured score improvements came from strategic reallocation of resources rather than genuine learning gains, demonstrating how metric design choices affect gaming incentives.},
